# Allowed SSH signers for git tag verification.
#
# Format (one signer per line):
#   <principal> namespaces="git" <ssh-key-type> <base64-key>
#
# The principal is a free-form identifier (email is conventional). The workflow
# verifies release tags against this list via:
#   git config gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile .github/allowed_signers
#   git tag -v "$GITHUB_REF_NAME"
#
# Replace the placeholder below with the maintainer's real SSH public key before
# the first publish. docs/publish-audit.md blocks the flip on this being done.
#
# maintainer@example.com namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAA...replace-me...
